# Resume Screening Web Application

## 📌 Project Overview
The Resume Screening Web Application is a Flask-based web project that helps automate the resume screening process using Machine Learning.  
It allows users to **register, login, upload resumes**, and view screening results through a simple and user-friendly interface.

This project demonstrates the integration of:
- Web development (Flask, HTML, CSS)
- Machine Learning model
- Database management
- User authentication

---

## 🛠️ Technologies Used
- Python
- Flask
- HTML, CSS
- Machine Learning (NLP-based resume screening)
- Git & GitHub

---

## 📂 Project Structure

RESUME_SCREENING/
│
├── app.py(copy and paste the code from app.py file)
├── model.py(copy and paste the code from "model.py" file)
├── database.db(copy and paste the code from "database.db" file)
├── requirements.txt(copy and paste the code from "requirements.txt" file)
│
├── static/
│ └── styles.css(copy and paste the code from "styles.css" file)
│
├── templates/
│ ├── login.html(copy and paste the code from "login.html" file)
│ ├── register.html(copy and paste the code from "register.html" file)
│ ├── dashboard.html(copy and paste the code from "dashboard.html" file)
│ └── result.html(copy and paste the code from "result.html" file)
│
├── instance/ # Auto-generated by Flask (configuration & runtime files)
├── pycache/ # Auto-generated by Python during execution

📌 **Note:**  
- `instance/` and `__pycache__/` folders are **automatically created** when the application runs and do not need to be manually added.

